From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 20:44:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: re-program colour-processing blocks on the
 commit after a modeset

On a modeset (resume, DPMS on, mode change) _dpu_crtc_setup_cp_blocks()
programs the DSPP before the first flush has activated it.  The plain
register writes (GC_EN, LUT_SWAP, PCC) stick, but the writes into the
SRAM-backed GC LUT through the index/data ports are lost.  The result on
a dual-LM panel with a GAMMA_LUT user (Hyprland + wlsunset) is gamma
enabled over uninitialised SRAM: a random colour tint / artifacts on one
half of the panel after every resume or DPMS off/on, cleared by any later
colour-management commit.

Register evidence on x1e80100 (DPU 9.2) eDP-1: bad vs good dumps of
dri/0/kms are identical except the GC block at dspp+0x17c0, where GC_EN=1
and the LUT data ports return garbage.

Remember that the CP blocks were programmed during a modeset and repeat
the programming on the next commit, once the pipeline is running.
Verified on Surface Pro 11: DPMS off/on 10/10 clean, previously defective
every cycle.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.h |  7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
index 42d0a529b4d5..3d1c138bfde8 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c
@@ -853,12 +853,24 @@ static void _dpu_crtc_setup_cp_blocks(struct drm_crtc *crtc)
 	struct dpu_hw_gc_lut *gc_lut;
 	struct dpu_hw_ctl *ctl;
 	struct dpu_hw_dspp *dspp;
+	struct dpu_crtc *dpu_crtc = to_dpu_crtc(crtc);
+	bool modeset = drm_atomic_crtc_needs_modeset(state);
 	int i;
 
 
-	if (!state->color_mgmt_changed && !drm_atomic_crtc_needs_modeset(state))
+	if (!state->color_mgmt_changed && !modeset &&
+	    !dpu_crtc->cp_reprogram_pending)
 		return;
 
+	/*
+	 * During a modeset the DSPP is programmed before the first flush
+	 * activates it, and writes into SRAM-backed sub-blocks (the GC LUT)
+	 * are lost while the enable bit sticks -- leaving the block enabled
+	 * over uninitialised SRAM.  Repeat the programming on the next commit,
+	 * once the pipeline is running.
+	 */
+	dpu_crtc->cp_reprogram_pending = modeset;
+
 	for (i = 0; i < cstate->num_mixers; i++) {
 		ctl = mixer[i].lm_ctl;
 		dspp = mixer[i].hw_dspp;
@@ -1240,6 +1252,7 @@ static void dpu_crtc_disable(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
 				atomic_read(&dpu_crtc->frame_pending));
 
 	trace_dpu_crtc_disable(DRMID(crtc), false, dpu_crtc);
+	dpu_crtc->cp_reprogram_pending = false;
 	dpu_crtc->enabled = false;
 
 	if (atomic_read(&dpu_crtc->frame_pending)) {
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.h
index 6eaba5696e8e..12c25bc860d3 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.h
@@ -165,6 +165,13 @@ struct dpu_crtc {
 	ktime_t vblank_cb_time;
 	bool enabled;
 
+	/*
+	 * Colour-processing blocks were programmed during a modeset, before
+	 * the DSPP was active; SRAM-backed sub-blocks (GC LUT) must be written
+	 * again on the next commit.
+	 */
+	bool cp_reprogram_pending;
+
 	struct list_head feature_list;
 	struct list_head active_list;
 	struct list_head dirty_list;
